WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.158
Digital artifacts feel concrete, but they still need context.

2
00:00:04.158 --> 00:00:15.246
A screenshot, log excerpt, alert, file name, message header, ticket note, or threat intelligence indicator may be useful evidence, yet each one is also

3
00:00:15.246 --> 00:00:17.556
a representation of something else.

4
00:00:17.556 --> 00:00:24.025
It may be filtered, cropped, transformed, copied, exported, summarized, or separated from surrounding events.

5
00:00:24.025 --> 00:00:30.031
Counter-deception asks how the artifact was collected and what it can actually prove.

6
00:00:30.031 --> 00:00:32.341
Provenance should be captured early.

7
00:00:32.341 --> 00:00:41.119
Analysts should record the source system, collector, collection time, time range, query or view used, and any transformation applied.

8
00:00:41.119 --> 00:00:52.207
Timestamps deserve special care because systems may use local time, UTC, different time zones, clock drift, ingestion delay, or display formatting that hides precision.

9
00:00:52.207 --> 00:00:59.599
A timeline built from mixed sources should explain those differences before drawing a conclusion from sequence.

10
00:00:59.599 --> 00:01:03.295
Screenshots and logs are common sources of confusion.

11
00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:14.384
A screenshot can preserve useful visual context, but it can omit browser state, account context, surrounding messages, or later changes in the system of

12
00:01:14.384 --> 00:01:14.846
record.

13
00:01:14.846 --> 00:01:25.934
A log line can confirm that an event was recorded, but it may not explain intent, user identity, session ownership, or whether related events

14
00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:28.244
were excluded by the query.

15
00:01:28.244 --> 00:01:32.402
The artifact supports only the claim it actually supports.

16
00:01:32.402 --> 00:01:36.098
Where possible, corroborate with independent telemetry or records.

17
00:01:36.098 --> 00:01:43.952
A suspicious account change might be checked against identity logs, approval tickets, device telemetry, and administrator actions.

18
00:01:43.952 --> 00:01:51.344
A claimed external indicator might be checked against original reporting, internal observations, and relevant time windows.

19
00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:58.737
Preserve evidence before drawing conclusions, maintain chain of custody for sensitive material, and document uncertainty plainly.

20
00:01:58.737 --> 00:02:03.819
Verification is strongest when artifact, context, and decision are tied together.
